{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the page stream fallback at head e10d7b9fa42e7831acce76e20bbdbe2b50d16878, tree c315929f16bdadb811d319211d43330197e09a79, for request 5874b15d and review request 46d9d783. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nThe head adds four commits to the reviewed head 33540f97. I read the implementation note's new \"Settings-loader review repair\" section first, then the diff from 33540f97, against item 1 of review c130edef. The rest of the head is unchanged, and the findings of c130edef on the client observer, the Page owner, the session checks, the Counter repair and the served witness stand.\n\n## Item 1 of c130edef\n\nResolved.\n\n- `settings()` in `apps/room/page/src/main.ts` now checks `pollIntervalMs` inside its own `try`. An invalid value leaves the field out, and the 5-second default applies. The place, the key and the stored bytes stay as they were. The other optional fields work the same way.\n- The Page journey in `page-observation.test.ts` runs three cases: a valid 1,000, an out-of-range 60,001, and the string `\"5000\"`. Each case checks that:\n  - the Page loads the original key and opens the original room;\n  - neither `saveSettings` nor `setItem` runs, and the stored record is byte-identical before and after;\n  - polling uses the effective interval, with no read before it and one read at it;\n  - the later comment renders, and a route change and retirement stop polling.\n- The control removes only the local catch. The unchanged named assertion then fails with an ordinary AssertionError because the key never loads, after valid setup. The helper restores the source bytes and mode.\n- `OBSERVE.md` says that an invalid stored interval uses the default without hiding or replacing the saved connection.\n- The first parameterized fixture failed to compile and to set up. Those failures stay recorded as failures.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 25930f62 gives a clean tree, 1e1b2d0c.\n- Gate 3 passes at a9d686b2, tree 5470ef15. Only the note and the manifest change from a9d686b2 to the head, which the documents-only rule covers. From 33540f97 to a9d686b2 the changes are `main.ts`, the regenerated `assets.ts`, the Page test, `OBSERVE.md` and the manifest.\n- I reran `apps/room/page/test/page-observation.test.ts` once, with no whole suite. It passes 6 of 6 tests, which matches `settings-page-owners-2`: 6 Page cases and 1 asset case.\n- The regenerated Page script is 13 bytes larger than the one the Mac witness served. As c130edef allowed, the head keeps that witness for valid settings and claims no new deployment or browser run. The repair changes only how the loader treats an invalid stored interval.\n- The manifest has SHA-256 bfbb1e0f and 58,382 bytes, and it names the continuation evidence directory. It follows ruling 4e199bd8:\n  - all 365 listed files match by size and SHA-256;\n  - `finalization` and `operator-inputs` match their digests, and each SHA256SUMS reruns clean, with no unlisted file;\n  - the root SHA256SUMS covers all 2,411 other files, with none unlisted and none writable.\n- The original evidence directory still verifies against its own SHA256SUMS.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 743 links, 0 broken.\n- check-notes from 14ffb0f6: one warning, for the 58,382-byte manifest over the soft limit, as disclosed. The implementation note is 40,126 bytes.\n- check-commit-messages from 14ffb0f6: 8 checked, 0 flagged.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\nThe two points of c130edef remain: the note names Chromium, and the healthy-stream case has only the scripted test.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe repair stays in the Page's settings loader. It changes no observer state, Worker route, stream wire or session rule. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nA bad optional value can no longer hide the member's stored connection or lead them to overwrite it. The journey proves that the stored bytes stay unchanged. The session, deployment and sending-fence findings of c130edef stand. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe repair is one local `try` that follows the loader's handling of its other optional fields, plus three test cases. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: item 1 holds in the source, the journey, the control and gate 3. The evidence verifies under ruling 4e199bd8, and the original evidence directory is unchanged.\n\nThe landing check will follow the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1e70229b19e90e2d03de0b1aacf2f77211056721","binding":"assigned","head":"e10d7b9fa42e7831acce76e20bbdbe2b50d16878","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e45381a09e44bb6a1a47d9924171985836b79a98\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:987563d7f9393ff6fc42aa477925bef2f78e5f24\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e45381a09e44bb6a1a47d9924171985836b79a98","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}